    "body": "COSCO Shipping ​​​​​​signed two logistics deals at a trade show in Shanghai on Nov. 6. One builds on its warehouse work with Western Post in Los Angeles. The other expands its work with Xiaomi in Panama, where a warehouse project has handled more than 1 million phones.\nWhat’s Related\nCOSCO Shipping North America signed a memorandum of understanding with Western Post (US) LLC at the China International Import Expo. COSCO Shipping Lines Central America signed a separate agreement with Xiaomi H.K. Limited at the same event.\n“Today's supply chains demand more than moving goods from one place to another. Customers need logistics partners who can connect transportation , warehousing and distribution into a seamless operation,” said Ma Jie, president of COSCO Shipping North America.\nWestern Post goes beyond warehousing\nCOSCO and Western Post began working together on warehousing in Los Angeles in 2024. Under the new agreement, they plan to better coordinate ocean shipments with warehousing and inland delivery for cross-border e-commerce customers.\nZe Kuaiyue, founder of AuGroup, said the companies would explore how to provide warehouse services for Chinese businesses expanding overseas. The agreement builds on the Los Angeles partnership by bringing the shipping and delivery legs into the work the companies already do together at the warehouse.\nXiaomi looks to expand past Panama\nCOSCO and Xiaomi plan to expand their work on warehouse management and order fulfillment , along with distribution across the region. They also plan to coordinate ocean and air shipments more closely with customs clearance and inland transportation. The agreement calls for exploring opportunities in North America and elsewhere in Latin America.\n“Building on our successful cooperation with COSCO SHIPPING in Panama, we look forward to leveraging COSCO SHIPPING’s global network and integrated supply chain capabilities to deliver reliable and efficient logistics solutions as we expand our regional footprint,” said Liu Cong, general manager of Xiaomi Group’s international delivery department.\nHow COSCO handles trans-Pacific orders\nAt the expo, COSCO Shipping North America demonstrated how it connects the steps involved in moving an e-commerce order across the Pacific. The demonstration showed how its systems link shipping and warehousing with final-mile delivery , the leg that takes a package to the customer.\nCOSCO also hosted a panel on AI in logistics. Participants from C.H. Robinson , Xiaomi, and other organizations discussed where AI could help with logistics decisions and where people still need to use their judgment.",
